# Excluded from the job's code snapshot.
#
# `code: .` uploads this directory. Without this file the snapshot would carry
# the local virtual environment (hundreds of MB), the dataset (which arrives
# through the data store, and shipping a second copy in the snapshot would let
# the job read the wrong one), and baseline.json (whose whole value is being
# computed independently of the job — a job that could see it is a job that
# could be accused of having used it).
#
# Azure ML falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, and the repository
# .gitignore lives at the root, outside the snapshot directory. So this file is
# not a convenience.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

data/
downloaded-model/
baseline.json

README.md
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
